    "created_at": "2018-10-15T18:59:39Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-10-15T18:59:39Z",
    "body": "Just a side note: `delegatesFocus` is a very bad property name for such init value IMHO. Do we have time to revisit it? I have found that this is particularly affecting folks with english as a second language. The most common mistake is forgetting the `s` from `delegates`, yes, it is a silly mistake, but nevertheless a mistake. Conjugation, declension and other grammatical rules are not very common in DOM APIs as far as I can remember, I wonder if this can be revisit, e.g. : (`activeFocus`, `focusDelegation` or `focusTransfer`)\r\n\r\nThis reminds me of some very interesting discussions that we had at TC39 a while ago about language APIs, and how they are perceived by a larger community of developers.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
